{
  "case_id": "2021-20-979",
  "document_hash": "c6cab9caa4685970cf65fae201c69d98e9a6936e81bf3d305db424705e1fe4ad",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-20-979",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c6cab9caa4685970cf65fae201c69d98e9a6936e81bf3d305db424705e1fe4ad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c6cab9caa468-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:00 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2021-20-979",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c6cab9caa4685970cf65fae201c69d98e9a6936e81bf3d305db424705e1fe4ad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c6cab9caa468-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument first this morning in Case 20-979, Patel versus Garland."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mark C. Fleming (Petitioners)",
      "case_id": "2021-20-979",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c6cab9caa4685970cf65fae201c69d98e9a6936e81bf3d305db424705e1fe4ad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c6cab9caa468-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "As the government agrees, section 1252(a)(2)(B)(i) does not bar review of the agency's threshold determination that Mr. Patel is ineligible for adjustment of status. That understanding is consistent with the statutory text, context, and history, and it's also consistent with this Court's explanation in Kucana that the (B)(i) bar is limited to decisions made discretionary by legislation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-979",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c6cab9caa4685970cf65fae201c69d98e9a6936e81bf3d305db424705e1fe4ad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c6cab9caa468-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Counsel, normally we review judgments or orders and not reasoning. It seems as though you're asking us to review reasoning as opposed to the order itself."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE KAGAN",
      "case_id": "2021-20-979",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c6cab9caa4685970cf65fae201c69d98e9a6936e81bf3d305db424705e1fe4ad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c6cab9caa468-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think, in response to Justice Alito's question, I'm -- I'm not sure why it matters to your position very much what the word \"judgment\" means, whether it means the final determination, the official order, or something else."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. FLEMING",
      "case_id": "2021-20-979",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c6cab9caa4685970cf65fae201c69d98e9a6936e81bf3d305db424705e1fe4ad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c6cab9caa468-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "As I understood your position, your position is just that the entire phrase \"judgment regarding the granting of relief\" refers to the step 2 determination rather than the step 1 determination, and whatever \"judgment\" means, whether it refers to the official order or some kind of discretionary decision-making along the way or both, your position would still stand, wouldn't it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "AUSTIN L. RAYNOR",
      "case_id": "2021-20-979",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c6cab9caa4685970cf65fae201c69d98e9a6936e81bf3d305db424705e1fe4ad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c6cab9caa468-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Section 1252(a)(2)(B) precludes review of any judgment regarding the granting of relief under five enumerated provisions, as well as any other decision or action of the Secretary or the Attorney General, the authority for which is specified to be in their discretion."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2021-20-979",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c6cab9caa4685970cf65fae201c69d98e9a6936e81bf3d305db424705e1fe4ad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c6cab9caa468-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I don't think Petitioners' position allows you to avoid this issue. They concede that certain eligibility criteria will be unreviewable under the second clause."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-20-979",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c6cab9caa4685970cf65fae201c69d98e9a6936e81bf3d305db424705e1fe4ad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c6cab9caa468-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: What is the mens rea requirement, if any, for the inadmissibility determination here?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-20-979",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c6cab9caa4685970cf65fae201c69d98e9a6936e81bf3d305db424705e1fe4ad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c6cab9caa468-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: If -- if Congress had thought that there was review of these sorts of factual issues, wouldn't it have been concerned in adding that provision that the implication was to the opposite effect?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2021-20-979",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c6cab9caa4685970cf65fae201c69d98e9a6936e81bf3d305db424705e1fe4ad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c6cab9caa468-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: Isn't that also mixed fact and -- but it also has some discretion mixed in?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Meehan",
      "case_id": "2021-20-979",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c6cab9caa4685970cf65fae201c69d98e9a6936e81bf3d305db424705e1fe4ad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c6cab9caa468-0002-0007",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There is not a lurking third exception for some findings of fact un-enumerated in either the jurisdictional bar or the exceptions clause. To say that there is would be contrary to the text of the statute, contrary to the structure of the statute, and contrary to one of IIRIRA's overarching purposes, to streamline judicial review, here, leaving fact-finding in the hands of the Executive Branch, consistent with historical practice."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Meehan",
      "case_id": "2021-20-979",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c6cab9caa4685970cf65fae201c69d98e9a6936e81bf3d305db424705e1fe4ad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c6cab9caa468-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 73,
        "start": 73
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And you're left with a clear -- you're left with a clear implication -- or, pardon, you're left with a clear conclusion that the jurisdictional bar must mean the overall denial of relief."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-20-979",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c6cab9caa4685970cf65fae201c69d98e9a6936e81bf3d305db424705e1fe4ad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c6cab9caa468-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 80,
        "start": 80
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Ms. -- Ms. --can I stop you there and just can I take you back to the basic question here, which is \"judgment regarding the granting of relief\" and what that phrase means."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KAVANAUGH",
      "case_id": "2021-20-979",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c6cab9caa4685970cf65fae201c69d98e9a6936e81bf3d305db424705e1fe4ad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c6cab9caa468-0004-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 87,
        "start": 87
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Can I pick up on your reference there to the government's argument and just get your reaction to what I think is the music of their argument?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "U.S. Government",
      "case_id": "2021-20-979",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c6cab9caa4685970cf65fae201c69d98e9a6936e81bf3d305db424705e1fe4ad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c6cab9caa468-0004-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 87,
        "start": 87
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So you have the '96 act and they agree with your position for the first five years. Then St. Cyr comes along, 2001, and the Bush Administration decides we need to interpret this statute in a way to avoid the constitutional problem, and they come up then, the government comes up with its current position, the discretionary position relying on the title and other things."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. MEEHAN",
      "case_id": "2021-20-979",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c6cab9caa4685970cf65fae201c69d98e9a6936e81bf3d305db424705e1fe4ad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c6cab9caa468-0004-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 88,
        "start": 88
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I don't think it's good enough for two reasons. First, it doesn't abide by the text, and, second, there are serious workability issues."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2021-20-979",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c6cab9caa4685970cf65fae201c69d98e9a6936e81bf3d305db424705e1fe4ad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c6cab9caa468-0004-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 95,
        "start": 95
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Petitioners' interpretation doesn't abide by the text and has arbitrariness problems. The government's interpretation doesn't abide by the text and has workability problems."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-20-979",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c6cab9caa4685970cf65fae201c69d98e9a6936e81bf3d305db424705e1fe4ad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c6cab9caa468-0004-0006",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 103,
        "start": 103
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
